Z||000000||Sevaan||03-22-2001||10:21 PM||||Hey guys,<P>Yesterday I wrote about a problem I had with engine stalls (http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009098.html). Please read for the background info.<P>Now, today I started the engine up cold and noted then pressed the diaphram under the EGR. The engine stalled, which means that the thing is working.<P>This means that I still haven't solved the problem. So:<P>Question #1: What's the problem?<P>In my exploratory poking I noted a few things with puzzlement and dismay. One: There is a pipe that comes out from under the fuel injector thing under the air cleaner. It's attached right above where the PCV pipe attaches. Now, I followed it and found that it wasn't connected anywhere. And even more alarming was that there was a screw and washer stuck into the open end to cap it off. I was able to pull the "cap" off without any effort, so I believe it was just shoved in there.<P>Question #2: What is this pipe and where does it lead?<P>Also, along the engine compartment at the rear of the vehicle, there is a pipe that is attached to the wall. You can see it easily (it runs perpendicular to the transmission fluid dipstick). I followed it to the right of the car and found it ends nowhere.<P>Question #3: What is this pipe?<P>Does the mystery injector pipe fit over this compartment pipe? Yes. But when I put it over and put the car into drive, the engine stalled immediately. When not attached it just idles really slow and then stalls.<P>So, any help an answers are appreciated. I can still drive the thing, but frequent stalls are really a pain, so I'd like to nurse my vehicle back to help.<P>Sorry for the long post.||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||03-22-2001||10:35 PM||||Now you got to tell us if this is a 4 or 6 cylinder. Too many things are different. I reviewed the last post and you don't say what it is there either.<p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 03-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-22-2001||10:37 PM||||whats the description of the two mystery pipes/hoses that you have found disconnected?<P>Is the hose coming from the throttle body a small one in diameter with larger diameter ends?  Is the "compartment" one kinda like a steel with what looks like a spring wrapped around it?  If it is a 4 cyl, I will look at mine tomorrow and see if I can see what you are seeing.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sevaan||03-22-2001||11:06 PM||||Sorry about that. It's a 4 cylinder automatic.<P>Pipe #1 is a one diameter black tube. No think or thin ends to it. It comes off the connector, under the injector, about 6 or 7 inches. It was tucked away under the PCV valve, which is probably why I never followed it to see where it lead. The only reason I discovered it today is that I removed the PVC to see if a vacuum tube was loose (it wasn't).<P>Pipe #2 is thin the steel one you're talking about.<P>Thanks for taking the time to read my messages. I appreciate all your help!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||03-23-2001||06:32 PM||||Pipe #1 is for the Thermac valve.<BR>Pipe #2 is for the vac canister.<BR>Pull the pipe off the TBI body and plug with a rubber cap.<BR>Now for the reality...<BR>Look at your deck lid, there should be a diagram of all the vac hoses...<BR>If not, get a manual.||||reg||1
